thHfG8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-swift-for-beginners-2026---lesson-8---logical-operators-ftwmvmamn","summary":"A beginner Swift lesson covering if, else if, and else statements. Explains how to evaluate boolean conditions and execute different code branches based on true/false results. Covers nested if statements, various forms of if statements (standalone, if-else, if-else if-else), and includes a practical temperature-based coding challenge. Also demonstrates Xcode's auto-indent feature.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EpC9EthHfG8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T13:39:02.000Z"},{"id":"zvVcIXgh0","title":"Learn Swift for Beginners 2026 - Lesson 7 - If, Else If, Else","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OGQvW-sQVoY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-swift-for-beginners-2026---lesson-7---if-else-if-else-zvvcixgh0","summary":"A beginner Swift tutorial covering if, else if, and else statements. Explains how conditional branches work, how Swift evaluates conditions top-to-bottom and skips remaining branches once a true condition is found, and demonstrates various forms including standalone if, if-else, multiple else-if chains, and nested if statements. Includes a practical temperature-classification coding challenge and tips for using Xcode's auto-indent feature.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/OGQvW-sQVoY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T13:24:04.000Z"},{"id":"pGZgwrAW1","title":"Learn Swift for Beginners 2026 - Lesson 6 - Comparison Operators","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=27zajydTlV8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-swift-for-beginners-2026---lesson-6---comparison-operators-pgzgwraw1","summary":"A beginner Swift lesson covering comparison operators including equal to (==), not equal to (!=), less than, greater than, and their or-equal-to variants. Demonstrates how comparisons evaluate to Boolean true/false values using a drinking age example. Includes a hands-on challenge to check password strength using the string .count property and the >= operator, with string interpolation to print results.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/27zajydTlV8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-24T13:00:11.000Z"},{"id":"KMNG5UwfO","title":"Learn Swift for Beginners 2026 - Lesson 5 - String Interpolation","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Yt1RBhPAyMk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-swift-for-beginners-2026---lesson-5---string-interpolation-kmng5uwfo","summary":"A beginner Swift lesson covering string interpolation, the technique of embedding variables and expressions directly inside string literals using the backslash-parentheses syntax. The lesson demonstrates inserting integers, doubles, booleans, and math expressions into strings, highlights a common mistake with forward slash, and ends with a hands-on challenge to build a welcome message using multiple variables.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Yt1RBhPAyMk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-23T15:32:33.000Z"},{"id":"by3FUZiRO","title":"How to reclaim disk space by deleting the DerivedData folder in macOS","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7br-66cfc68","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/mac-running-out-of-space-check-xcode-macstorage-xcode-cleanup-by3fuziro","summary":"Over time, the DerivedData folder in macOS can accumulate up to 126 GB of build artifacts from compiling and running projects. This folder can be safely deleted to reclaim disk space without any lasting harm to your projects.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/7br-66cfc68/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-22T18:46:18.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["prettier","liveoverflow","blackthornprod","appledeveloper","codingwithsphere"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","kloss_xyz","ryolu_","patrickc"],"similar":[{"id":"pr